// src/elevate.pdx — umount.pdxfs.M1-001 (scaffold) — elevate placeholder
//
// design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §5.2 + §8.2 describe umount.pdxfs's
// `--force` gate: forcing an unmount past the "handles still open"
// refusal (§5.3) requires a `KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL` grant when the
// resolved mount point falls under `/system`, `/boot`, or `/dev`
// (mirrors mount.pdxfs's own §4.2 mount-point-class table). This file
// is the placeholder this issue's own instruction names for that future
// work -- it declares no live entry point at M1, since:
//
//   (a) main.pdx never reaches a --force code path at M1 (the only
//       branches wired are the argv-missing-target diagnostic, the
//       --dry-run record emit, and the generic "not yet implemented"
//       fallthrough -- --force is parsed into ParsedArgv.flags by
//       argv.pdx but never inspected by main.pdx's M1 _start), and
//   (b) `libpdx-elevate` has not been located anywhere under
//       paideia-satellites/ as of this landing (a `grep -rl
//       libpdx-elevate` across the paideia-os monorepo and every
//       satellite repo finds zero implementation files) -- the same
//       "design-doc-mentioned, not yet bootstrapped" status
//       mkfs.pdxfs's own design/architecture.md §9 documents for
//       `libpdx-elevate` ahead of that tool's own M3-005. See
//       design/architecture.md §3 in this repo for the full note.
//
// What lands here, and when:
//
//   umount.pdxfs.M3-002 ("--force path: libpdx-elevate + handle-revoke
//   + revoked_handles list in record") is where this file grows a real
//   `elevate_request_force_unmount(mount_point_ptr) -> u64` entry point
//   -- requesting a `KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL` grant scoped to the resolved
//   mount point, blocking (or consulting the `elevate_policy.pdx`
//   auto-approve table per §8.2) until APPROVED/DENIED/EXPIRED, and
//   returning a status main.pdx gates the handle-revoke sequence on. If
//   `libpdx-elevate` still does not exist by the time M3-002 opens,
//   this file implements a minimal inline fallback instead (same
//   "check for the library, ship inline if absent" posture argv.pdx
//   takes for `libpdx-argv` at M1) -- confirm with main before that
//   issue opens, per design/architecture.md §3's own flag.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// umount.pdxfs.M3-002 (#8) landing: fail-closed STUB, not a real
// libpdx-elevate acquire+require sequence -- same posture mkfs.pdxfs's
// M3-005 (#12) elevate_wire.pdx documents in full
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// `libpdx-elevate` (paideia-satellites/libpdx-elevate) DOES now exist
// as a real, mature library -- unlike the "not yet bootstrapped" status
// this file's M1 header described. But its real, landed API
// (`elevate_client_acquire(caps, dur, req_buf, reply_ep_id, reply_buf,
// mint_ctx_buf) -> row_id`) REQUIRES the caller to already hold a
// `KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT` cap over the elevate broker, supplied as
// `parent_ep_slot` inside a caller-populated 40-byte `mint_ctx_buf`.
// `libpdx-elevate`'s own `caps.decl`/README are explicit that this
// prerequisite cap is "declared by whatever the caller links this
// library into, not by libpdx-elevate" itself. `umount.pdxfs` has no
// such cap: this repo's own `caps.decl` (M1 landing, unchanged since)
// declares `KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL` as a placeholder only -- no design
// doc or osarch coordination point has minted this tool a real broker
// endpoint. Without `parent_ep_slot`, there is no honest way to
// construct a real `elevate_client_acquire` call -- fabricating one
// against fields this repo cannot legitimately populate would look
// real without being real (the exact trap `src/target_resolve.pdx`'s
// own module header documents avoiding for its mount-table row).
//
// `elevate_request_force_unmount` below therefore ALWAYS returns
// `ELEV_DENY` -- an honest, fail-closed answer to "can this process
// prove it holds elevation to force-unmount past open handles", since
// "cannot construct a real request" and "cannot prove GRANT" collapse
// to the same externally observable outcome. `ELEV_GRANT` and the
// caller-side GRANT arm (`src/unmount_op.pdx`'s handle-revoke stub) are
// real, wired code paths kept for the day a broker-endpoint cap exists
// -- only this function's body needs to change to a real
// `elevate_client_acquire` + `elevate_client_require` sequence.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Encoder-gap discipline
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// No `add reg, [mem]` anywhere. No `test` mnemonic. Pure leaf: no
// branch, no label needed.
//
// Upstream: design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §5.2 + §8.2 (paideia-os);
// paideia-satellites/libpdx-elevate README.md "Callers" section +
// caps.decl (the parent_ep_slot prerequisite); mkfs.pdxfs's own
// src/elevate_wire.pdx (M3-005, #12 -- the identical fail-closed
// posture over the identical missing-broker-cap gap).

module Elevate = structure {

  // KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL = 0x191 (src/kernel/core/cap/kind_elevate_channel.pdx,
  // R48b, derived over KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT base 5). Referenced here purely
  // as documentation cross-reference; not consumed by any code path in
  // this file (see caps.decl's own note on the same kind).
  pub let KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL_REF : u64 = 0x191

  // --- elevate_request_force_unmount return values. -----------------------
  //
  // PFS-15 (paideia-os#2582) ADDED a third sentinel, ELEV_NO_SLOT (2):
  // distinguishes "we asked the broker and it denied" (ELEV_DENY) from
  // "we have no broker-endpoint cap to ask through at all" (ELEV_NO_SLOT).
  // The surface difference matters for the operator-visible exit code:
  // ELEV_DENY -> UMOUNT_ERR_REVOKE_FAIL (the broker said no), ELEV_NO_SLOT
  // -> UMOUNT_ERR_NO_ELEVATE (the tool was never provisioned a broker).
  // ELEV_NO_SLOT is the ONLY reachable value today, matching mint.pdxfs's
  // own `mount_mw_elevate_slot` default-zero posture (src/mint_wire.pdx);
  // ELEV_DENY and ELEV_GRANT are real, wired code paths kept for the day
  // PFS-02's `_init_caps` seed convention lands kernel-side and the
  // broker-endpoint cap arrives at slot 5.
  pub let ELEV_DENY     : u64 = 0
  pub let ELEV_GRANT    : u64 = 1
  pub let ELEV_NO_SLOT  : u64 = 2

  // --- PFS-15: broker-endpoint cap slot, mint_wire pattern. ---------------
  //
  // PFS-02 (`design/pdxfs/init-caps-seed-convention.md` §2.3, paideia-os
  // repo) names slot 5 as the canonical `_init_caps` seed slot for a
  // pdxfs tool's KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT handle on `svc.elevate-broker`
  // (ELEVATE_BROKER_ENDPOINT_ID = 16). Until PFS-02's kernel-side
  // enablement wave lands (grow KIND_SEEDABLE_TABLE, singleton-row mint
  // path, broker-endpoint seed-time gate -- tracked at paideia-os
  // follow-up), this `.bss` u64 stays zero and every elevate call
  // refuses with ELEV_NO_SLOT (fail-closed). The slot number is the
  // SAME number mint.pdxfs's own `mount_mw_elevate_slot` reserves (see
  // src/mint_wire.pdx in that repo) -- a single ambient seed slot
  // across every pdxfs CLI tool, by the design-doc convention.
  //
  // Future real body (unchanged signature, body-only edit) once PFS-02
  // closes:
  //
  //   mov rax, [rip + umnt_elev_broker_slot];
  //   cmp rax, 0;
  //   je no_slot_arm;
  //   // Build the libpdx-elevate 40-byte mint_ctx_buf (parent_ep_slot =
  //   // rax; caps = KIND_VOLUME | R_VOL_REVOKE; dur = default; …); call
  //   // elevate_client_acquire; branch on APPROVED/DENIED/EXPIRED.
  //
  pub let LPX_SEED_SLOT_ELEVATE_EP : u64 = 5
  pub let mut umnt_elev_broker_slot : u64 = uninit @align(8)

  // ==========================================================================
  // elevate_request_force_unmount(mount_id) -> u64
  //   (ELEV_DENY | ELEV_GRANT -- see module header: DENY is the only
  //   value this landing's body can ever produce)
  //
  //   rdi = mount_id  (unused by this landing's body -- kept as a
  //                     parameter so a future real body has it
  //                     available without an ABI change, since a real
  //                     elevate_client_acquire call would need it for
  //                     audit/logging context)
  //
  // Pure leaf, no branches, no nested call, no push/pop.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let elevate_request_force_unmount : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (mount_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "umount.pdxfs.M3-002 (#8) + PFS-15 (paideia-os#2582): elevate_request_force_unmount entry point. PFS-15 rewrite reuses mount.pdxfs's mint_wire pattern (src/mint_wire.pdx `mount_mw_elevate_slot`): read [rip+umnt_elev_broker_slot] into rax; cmp rax,0; je umnt_elev_force_no_slot -> `mov rax, 2` (ELEV_NO_SLOT); ret. Nonzero slot: ELEV_GRANT (1) today -- the real body would issue libpdx-elevate's elevate_client_acquire for (KIND_VOLUME, R_VOL_REVOKE, mount_id) and branch APPROVED/DENIED/EXPIRED, but PFS-02's kernel-side seed enablement is still open, so no slot is ever provisioned at this landing and the GRANT arm is unreachable. mount_id (rdi) is accepted and read into r11 only so a future real elevate_client_acquire has it in a callee-save slot (per mint_wire's own `rbx = dev_cap` convention); no push/pop needed because r11 is caller-save and the only nested work (future-elevate call) runs on the GRANT arm which rewrites r11 anyway. Pure leaf today. No `add reg,[mem]`, no `test`. Labels prefixed umnt_elev_force_.",
      block: {
        mov r11, rdi;                        // mount_id (reserved for future elevate_client_acquire)
        mov rax, [rip + umnt_elev_broker_slot];
        cmp rax, 0;
        je umnt_elev_force_no_slot;

        // Slot provisioned -> ELEV_GRANT today (unreachable at this
        // landing; see module header for the real elevate_client_acquire
        // sequence that replaces this body once PFS-02 seeds the slot).
        mov rax, 1;                          // ELEV_GRANT
        ret;

      umnt_elev_force_no_slot:
        mov rax, 2;                          // ELEV_NO_SLOT (fail-closed; the only reachable value)
        ret;
      }
    }

  // ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  // umount.pdxfs.LE-001 (#22) — SECOND, independent elevate gate:
  // /system unmount, regardless of --force/--lazy/handle_count
  // ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  // `elevate_request_force_unmount` above gates `--force` past an
  // IN_USE (open-handle) refusal -- it is only ever reached from
  // `unmount_op.pdx`'s own handle_count>0 branch. LE-001's own
  // acceptance criteria ask for a DIFFERENT, orthogonal gate: unmounting
  // ANY target whose raw argv string classifies as `/system` (per
  // `TargetResolve::target_is_system`, src/target_resolve.pdx) must
  // acquire elevation BEFORE the mount-table mutation runs -- even when
  // handle_count == 0 and neither `--force` nor `--lazy` is set, the
  // ONLY reachable arm of `unmount_op`'s own force/lazy gate at this
  // landing (see that file's own module header). These two gates are
  // genuinely independent predicates (open-handle-and-forcing vs.
  // target-classification) over independent call chains; this function
  // is the second one, not a refactor of the first.
  //
  // Same fail-closed posture as `elevate_request_force_unmount` above
  // and mount.pdxfs's own `Elevate::mount_elev_require_system`: the
  // real, landed `libpdx-elevate.ElevateClientAcquire::elevate_client_
  // acquire(caps, dur, req_buf, reply_ep_id, reply_buf, mint_ctx_buf) ->
  // row_id` entry point REQUIRES the caller to already hold a `KIND_
  // IPC_ENDPOINT` cap over `svc.elevate-broker` at `mint_ctx_buf.
  // parent_ep_slot` -- a prerequisite this repo's own `caps.decl`
  // (unchanged since the R90-XREPO.013.M4-001 adoption pass) is
  // explicit is NOT held: no code path in this repo has ever bound a
  // real broker-endpoint cap, and no design doc or osarch coordination
  // point has since minted `umount.pdxfs` one. Fabricating a `mint_ctx_
  // buf.parent_ep_slot` value this repo cannot honestly populate would
  // look real without being real -- the exact trap this file's own M1
  // header (above) already documents avoiding for the `--force` gate.
  //
  // `elevate_request_system_unmount` below therefore ALWAYS returns
  // `ELEV_DENY` -- an honest, fail-closed answer to "can this process
  // prove it holds elevation to unmount a /system target". Per LE-001's
  // own acceptance criteria ("Elevate refused -> umount exits non-zero,
  // mount stays live"), the caller (`src/main.pdx`) treats `ELEV_DENY`
  // as a hard stop BEFORE `HandleCheck::handle_check_refuse` or
  // `UnmountOp::unmount_op` is ever called -- no mutation of any kind
  // is attempted on this arm. `ELEV_GRANT` and the caller-side GRANT
  // arm (`src/main.pdx`'s own dispatch) are real, wired code paths kept
  // for the day a broker-endpoint cap exists -- only THIS function's
  // body needs to change, to a real `elevate_client_acquire` (before
  // the mutation) + `elevate_client_require` (immediately before the
  // kernel op) + `elevate_client_cap_check_and_revoke` (on completion)
  // sequence, per LE-001's own desired end-state. No caller-side ABI
  // change is needed for that day to arrive.
  //
  // Pure leaf, no branches, no nested call, no push/pop.
  // ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  // Upstream: design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §5.2, §8.2
  // (paideia-os); paideia-os/umount.pdxfs#22 (LE-001); paideia-satellites/
  // libpdx-elevate README.md "Callers" section + caps.decl (the parent_
  // ep_slot prerequisite); mount.pdxfs's own src/elevate.pdx (`mount_
  // elev_require_system` -- the sibling-repo precedent this function's
  // fail-closed posture and write-up mirror); src/target_resolve.pdx
  // (this repo, `target_is_system` -- the predicate this gate is keyed
  // on).
  // ==========================================================================
  // elevate_request_system_unmount(mount_point_ptr) -> u64
  //     (ELEV_DENY | ELEV_GRANT -- see doc comment above: DENY is the
  //     only value this landing's body can ever produce)
  //
  //   rdi = mount_point_ptr  (unused by this landing's body -- kept as a
  //                           parameter so a future real elevate_client_
  //                           acquire call has it available without an
  //                           ABI change, for audit/logging context)
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let elevate_request_system_unmount : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (mount_point_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "umount.pdxfs.LE-001 (#22): elevate_request_system_unmount entry point. mount_point_ptr (rdi) is accepted but READ BY NOTHING in this landing's body -- see this function's own doc comment for why no real elevate_client_acquire/elevate_client_require call can be honestly constructed yet (no broker-endpoint cap in this tool's caps.decl). `mov rax, 0` (ELEV_DENY; fail-closed) unconditionally; `ret`. Pure leaf -- no push/pop, no `add reg,[mem]`, no `test`. No labels needed (no branch).",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0;                          // ELEV_DENY (fail-closed; see doc comment above)
        ret;
      }
    }
}
